cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this corpus, cite it as below. The transcripts themselves are the
  Argentine Senate's and are cited separately, by sitting date and the
  per-sitting URL in raw_data_manifest.csv; see docs/RELEASE.md.
title: >-
  Argentine Senate stenographic transcripts, 2000-2024: a speaker-attributed
  corpus
abstract: >-
  Every stenographic record (version taquigrafica) the Argentine Senate serves
  for its sittings from February 2000 to December 2024, parsed from the
  chamber's own PDFs into speaker-attributed passages: 559 sittings, 233,408
  rows, 151,761 passages of speech and 31,955 typed stenographer's notes,
  21.46 million words. Each passage carries the printed speaker label, the
  senator it resolves to and the caucus that senator sat with on the day. The
  source PDFs are not redistributed: a manifest identifies each one by SHA-256
  and source URL, and the downloader in the repository fetches them again. The
  derived tables and reference data are CC BY 4.0; the code that produces them
  is MIT.
type: dataset
version: 0.4.37
date-released: '2026-09-08'
license: CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - family-names: Ripamonti
    given-names: Juan
keywords:
  - Argentina
  - Senate
  - parliamentary debate
  - legislative speech
  - stenographic transcripts
  - text as data
  - Spanish
  - political science
  - digital humanities
identifiers:
